msgid "projects.adhd-materia.short-desc"
msgstr "Python-scriptable task manager for programmers"

msgid "projects.adhd-materia.long-desc"
msgstr ""
"Task management software scriptable using python, over-engineered with love for "
"programmers\n"
"\n"
"[ul]\n"
"Make tasks with name, a description, and a list of tags\n"
"Tags can contain values that can be read from python scripts: text, numbers, calendar "
"dates, references to tasks, other tags, list, dictionaries, etc.\n"
"Put sub-tasks within tasks (a sub-task can even have multiple parent tasks)\n"
"Auto-scheduling and repeating tasks\n"
"Make custom python filters and sort based on tags and their values\n"
"Made in 2 weeks in Rust + egui, for fun\n"
"Was useful to me during my [color=#97fff6][url={\"project\": \"uid://"
"bc4mi6sb8bskl\"}]apprenticeship at Dada! Animation[/url][/color]\n"
"[/ul]\n"
"\n"
"Tags can contain values like strings, numbers, dates, lists, string-keyed dictionaries, "
"other tags, and references to tasks. Python scripts to filter and sort tasks can access "
"these tags. One of the default tags is [code]priority(<string>)[/code], which supports "
"setting priorities like A, B, C-, S++, etc.\n"
"One of the default sorting scripts sorts tasks based on this priority tag. Multiple "
"sorting scripts can be enabled at once with an order of execution.\n"
"Tasks within tasks are actually implemented using tags. A [code]subtask-of(<task-id>)[/"
"code] tag is inserted into sub-tasks, pointing to the parent task. The default python "
"filter only shows them when looking inside the parent task. This means a sub-task can "
"technically have multiple parents, or even be its own parent (why would anyone do that is "
"another question).\n"
"These is indeed very over-engineered and wasn't necessarily done out of efficiency, but "
"it was enjoyable to make and that was the goal."

msgid "projects.dada.name"
msgstr "Tool Developer at Dada! Animation"

msgid "projects.dada.short-desc"
msgstr "Pipeline integration in Unity/Unreal, general tooling"

msgid "projects.dada.long-desc"
msgstr ""
"Dada! Animation is an animation studio, in which I worked as a tool developer.\n"
"\n"
"[font_size=30]My Role[/font_size]\n"
"[ul]\n"
"Automation of repetitive tasks for artists\n"
"Automatic creation of project structures\n"
"Automatic retrieval and placement of assets made by other artists in a scene, from the "
"company database\n"
"Detection of new asset versions pushed by other artists, and the ability to swap them "
"directly inside the project\n"
"Many new automations in their existing Unity tools, and brand new Unreal tools built in "
"Rust\n"
"Custom fork on the Unity Recorder to improve its performance, making it multithreaded "
"(~30% improvement in render times)\n"
"A lot of unit-test creation and overall cleanup of the architecture to improve future "
"maintainability\n"
"Small external tools for other needs, generally made in Rust (bulk unity project updater, "
"custom project launcher, etc.)\n"
"[/ul]"

msgid "projects.dialog-tool.name"
msgstr "Dialogue Tool for Unreal"

msgid "projects.dialog-tool.short-desc"
msgstr "Node-based tool made in Godot to make dialogues for an Unreal game"

msgid "projects.dialog-tool.long-desc"
msgstr ""
"[font_size=30]My Work[/font_size]\n"
"[ul]\n"
"Node-based branching dialogue creation\n"
"Custom player choices\n"
"Pre-create characters with visual distinction inside the tool\n"
"Trigger events from dialog\n"
"Exports to a [code].csv[/code] Unreal can translate to a table, which I then load to "
"display dialogues\n"
"Made for [color=#97fff6][url={\"project\": \"uid://cob6f6sh4070u\"}]Kokopelli[/url][/"
"color]\n"
"Made a about a week during pre-production\n"
"Was very useful to the game designers for the whole production\n"
"[/ul]\n"
"\n"
"[font_size=30]Why Godot?[/font_size]\n"
"\n"
"Godot is very well [b]adapted to tool development[/b]. It is the reason I could make this "
"tool in a week: it allowed me to focus on the features of the tool, with much less "
"boilerplate work than if I needed to integrate the tool directly into Unreal.\n"
"The export logic is very simple, only going through a [code].csv[/code] that can be "
"export with a [b]quick keyboard shortcut[/b], so the time gain was very [b]worth it[/b]."

