msgid "projects.holodia.name"
msgstr "Gameplay Programmer at Holodia"

msgid "projects.holodia.short-desc"
msgstr "VR gameplay, character customization, juiciness"

msgid "projects.holodia.long-desc"
msgstr ""
"Holodia is a studio that maintains Holofit, a VR fitness game that can connect to your "
"fitness devices allow you to move through virtual environments.\n"
"\n"
"[font_size=30]My Role[/font_size]\n"
"[ul]\n"
"Character customization system, where cosmetics can be added over time in live service\n"
"Boss-fight in VR pass-through, with patterns that force the player to move their body\n"
"Quality of life features\n"
"Many bug fixes\n"
"Rendering optimizations\n"
"[/ul]"

msgid "projects.hyper-balls.short-desc"
msgstr "Golf puzzle game made in 10 days"

msgid "projects.hyper-balls.long-desc"
msgstr ""
"[ul]\n"
"Golf-like game\n"
"Zone with effects (acceleration/deceleration, death, pushing)\n"
"Logic puzzles: put balls in zones to activate/deactivate other zones or walls\n"
"Every hole needs one ball\n"
"Undo/redo\n"
"Made in a 10 days time constraint\n"
"10 levels (3 tutorial + 7 regular)\n"
"Satisfying sound design\n"
"First game I actually published\n"
"[/ul]\n"
"\n"
"[font_size=30]Things to improve[/font_size]\n"
"[ul]\n"
"Not enough levels\n"
"Level design could be better\n"
"Difficulty curve is too steep\n"
"[/ul]"

msgid "projects.kokopeli.short-desc"
msgstr "RPG vertical-slice made at Isart"

msgid "projects.kokopeli.long-desc"
msgstr ""
"An RPG vertical slice made at Isart Digital with 20 people (gameplay progs, engine progs, "
"artists, game designers, sound designers)\n"
"\n"
"[font_size=30]My Role[/font_size]\n"
"[ul]\n"
"See the [color=#97fff6][url={\"project\": \"uid://p0e4721sun7c\"}]node-based dialog tool[/"
"url][/color] I made for it\n"
"Camera system with various level design tools to position/rotate it in different parts of "
"the level design\n"
"Inventory system and UI\n"
"Dialogue UI with 2D rigged animations for characters\n"
"Some particle effects and juiciness\n"
"[/ul]\n"
"\n"
"[font_size=30]The Game[/font_size]\n"
"\n"
"Kokopelli is a turn-based RPG taking place in Albuquerque, USA.\n"
"\n"
"You embody the member of a Spirit Brigade in charge of befriending spirits in a world in "
"which humans and spirits live in harmony.\n"
"\n"
"The combat gameplay opposes the player to a spirit. They both have [b]dolls[/b], and make "
"use of [b]dice[/b], that each opponent throws to [b]attack[/b], [b]heal[/b], or do others "
"actions. There are [b]5 turns[/b], and the one who [b]killed the most dolls at the end "
"wins[/b]. The catch is that, the fights are very hard, and barely winnable. So to win, "
"you actually have to [b]cheat[/b]."

msgid "projects.pfe.short-desc"
msgstr "Car combat, end-of-studies project"

msgid "projects.pfe.long-desc"
msgstr ""
"Car combat game with a grappling hook. Grapple onto enemies and charge at them, or "
"grapple onto grapple-points in the world.\n"
"\n"
"[font_size=30]My Role[/font_size]\n"
"[ul]\n"
"The entire UI\n"
"The settings\n"
"A game-flow system to easily change the flow between different states of the game (menu, "
"game). Was useful because of many changes in the game design over production\n"
"Shaders and VFX\n"
"Player aim-assist\n"
"Enemy AI architecture\n"
"[/ul]"

msgid "projects.salty-ghosts.short-desc"
msgstr "Your projectiles hurt both the enemies and yourself"

msgid "projects.salty-ghosts.long-desc"
msgstr ""
"Submission for the [color=#97fff6][url={\"url\": \"https://itch.io/jam/mini-jam-117-"
"ghosts\"}]Mini Jam 117[/url][/color].\n"
"\n"
"[ul]\n"
"Shoot enemy ghosts with salt to hurt them. But you are a ghost too, so the salt hurts you "
"as well\n"
"Basic enemy that pursues you\n"
"Repulsor enemy that creates replusions. The repulsions don't hurt you directly, but they "
"push the salt piles around\n"
"Tornado enemy that throws tornadoes at you. Same as above, they don't hurt you directly, "
"but they catch the salt in their path\n"
"You have a dash that allows you to go through salt, with a cooldown\n"
"6 levels, and a boss level\n"
"Boss with patterns that are harder versions of the previous enemies\n"
"72 hours game jam\n"
"2 programmers, 1 artist\n"
"[/ul]\n"
"\n"
"The game was ranked [b]#2 out of 190 in enjoyment[/b], and [b]#9 overall[/b]."

msgid "projects.ultra-rising.name"
msgstr "Hack and Slash"

msgid "projects.ultra-rising.short-desc"
msgstr "Fast paced hack and slash prototype"

msgid "projects.ultra-rising.long-desc"
msgstr ""
"[ul]\n"
"Focused on game feel and fluidity of gameplay\n"
"Blade combat with combos\n"
"Can launch and juggle enemies mid-air\n"
"Advanced movement tech inspired by Celeste\n"
"[/ul]\n"
"\n"
"[font_size=30]Things to improve[/font_size]\n"
"[ul]\n"
"Not enough control over your actions as player, it feels like the best move is to spam "
"every move.\n"
"Not enough distinction between entities in the air and on the ground\n"
"...the graphics\n"
"[/ul]"
